From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christophe Pettus <xof@thebuild.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 13:34:23 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 25/35] H15: charge hayro-jpeg2000's declared-size allocations
 to a per-decode budget

hayro_jpeg2000::DecodeSettings gains max_memory_bytes. Image::new prices
the tile records from the header (one Tile per tile, each with a copy of
every component's parameters) and refuses a header whose records alone
exceed the limit; the tile count becomes checked arithmetic. Each decode
starts a fresh budget in its DecoderContext and charges, before
allocating: the tile records, the channel planes (palette-indexed images
included), the coefficient buffer, the precinct, code-block, layer and
tag-tree records, the position-progression precinct list, the code-block
and IDWT buffers, the output buffer and the palette-resolved planes.
Reused buffers grow through reserves that charge exactly the capacity
they add. A refusal is ValidationError::MemoryBudget.

hayro-syntax passes 64 bytes per pixel of max_image_pixels in both
DecodeSettings it builds and maps the refusal to
DecodeFailure::ImageMemoryLimit, counted in image_memory_limit_hits().
